      "FacilityID": 1000118288,
      "SummaryText": "Risk Management Plan - Executive Summary\n\nFacility:  MFA Agri Service Pattonsburg\nLocation:  204 W 1st Street Pattonsburg, MO 64670\nContact:  Aaron Easley\nPhone:  660-367-4311\n\n1.  The Facility Policy\n\nMFA Incorporated and the employees of MFA Agri Service Pattonsburg are committed to the prevention of any accidental release of anhydrous  ammonia.  If an accidental release should occur, the facility is prepared to work with the Daviess County LEPC and other authorities to mitigate any release and minimize the impact of any release to people and the environment.\n\n2.  Stationary Source and Regulated Substance Handled\n\nThe facility operates an anhydrous ammonia nurse tank storage facility and sells the regulated substance, anhydrous ammonia, for direct application as a crop nutrient.\n\n3.  The Accidental Release Prevention Program\n\nThe Accidental Release Prevention Program for the location consists of following the provisions of:\na.\t40 CFR Part 68\nb.\tOSHA 29 CFR 1910.111\nc.\tMissouri Anhydrous Ammonia  Law\nd.\tCGA G.2.1 \u0096 2023      \n\n4. The Five-year Accident History\n\nThis is a first time registration as an RMP facility.\n\n5. The Emergency Response Program\n\nThe facility has;\n\na. a written emergency action plan, in accordance with OSHA Standard, 29 CFR 1910.38;\n\nb. provided State and Local authorities with the emergency planning and community\n     right-to-know information as required under SARA Title III (EPCRA);\n\nc. employees will not respond to any release, local responders will be notified to control any \n     release.\n\n6.  Planned Changes to Improve Safety\n\nSafety improvement is an on-going process at the facility.  Periodic evaluations are performed to assess the condition and operation of the facility and improvements are made where warranted.\n\n10/30/2025"
    }
  ]
